{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The bug was `int(p / 100 * n)` truncating the rank, which overshoots by one and indexes out of range at `p=100`. Now `percentile` computes the proper nearest-rank:\n\n```8:14:/Users/psudokit/benchmark/runs/20260928-195007-g2-kimi-k3-T004-percentile-nearest-rank-r0/work/repo/stats.py\n    ordered = sorted(values)\n    n = len(ordered)\n    # Nearest-rank: rank = ceil(p/100 * n), clamped to [1, n]; index is rank - 1.\n    rank = math.ceil(p / 100 * n)\n    rank = min(max(rank, 1), n)\n    return ordered[rank - 1]\n```\n\n- `p=0` → rank clamped to 1 → minimum\n- `p=100` → rank = n → maximum (no out-of-range)\n- `p=50` of 1..10 → rank 5 → value 5\n\nTests pass: `2 passed` (note: only `python3` is on PATH here, not `python`)."}]},"session_id":"5d0e3ea0-3542-408c-8b5e-b10db7e8c63a"}
